       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit. A dose this high also raises the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the label:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg once or twice daily:** I can enter this if the 1,700 mg figure was meant as a total daily dose. For example, 850 mg twice daily is 1,700 mg/day.\n- **A lower starting dose:** Typical starts are 500 mg twice daily or 850 mg once daily with meals, titrated up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, or confirm the intended total daily dose, and I'll enter it."
      }
